*> Helpers of the tint tests (docs/protocol/43-tint-sources.md). COPY it after the test program.
*>   TINT-HEX-OF USING value (BINARY-DOUBLE, 0..4294967295), text (PIC X(8)): the value as eight
*>     upper-case hex digits (an ARGB colour as the document writes it).
*>   TINT-CHECK USING case (PIC X(240)), expected (PIC X(8)), value: one TEST line comparing the hex.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TINT-HEX-OF.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-HEXDIGITS           PIC X(16) VALUE "0123456789ABCDEF".
 01 WS-V                   BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-D                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-VALUE                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 L-TEXT                 PIC X(8).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-VALUE L-TEXT.
     MOVE L-VALUE TO WS-V
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 8 BY -1 UNTIL WS-I < 1
         COMPUTE WS-D = FUNCTION MOD(WS-V, 16)
         MOVE WS-HEXDIGITS(WS-D + 1:1) TO L-TEXT(WS-I:1)
         COMPUTE WS-V = WS-V / 16
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TINT-HEX-OF.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TINT-CHECK.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-OBS                 PIC X(8).
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-CASE                 PIC X(240).
 01 L-EXPECTED             PIC X(8).
 01 L-VALUE                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-CASE L-EXPECTED L-VALUE.
     MOVE L-CASE TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE L-EXPECTED TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TINT-HEX-OF" USING L-VALUE WS-OBS
     MOVE WS-OBS TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TINT-CHECK.
